OpenArena (apps/openarena)

Engine (engine/)
  ioquake3, by the ioquake3 contributors, based on the Quake III Arena
  source code by id Software (1999-2005).
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any
  later version (engine/COPYING.txt).
  Source: https://github.com/ioquake/ioq3, commit
  87a99d18206e878a20289f05ac3c16005dcae5c3, with frunk.store's changes for
  the browser in engine/ioq3-web.patch (also tools/openarena/ioq3-web.patch
  in https://github.com/RobertPKyle/frunk-store, whose
  tools/build-openarena.mjs builds it). The complete patched source the
  build came from is engine/ioq3-87a99d18206e-web-src.tar.gz.
  The changes: walking, turning and looking handed in by the page, its
  console commands, keys and menu pointer, the game's state for the page,
  saving the settings from the page, keys only while the game has the
  focus, and the screen-space ambient occlusion, depth blur and sun shadow
  shaders built only when those effects are on (in Chrome on ANGLE's Vulkan
  backend the graphics process crashed after linking them).

Game (data/)
  OpenArena 0.8.8, by the OpenArena team and contributors (data/CREDITS,
  data/README, data/readme_085.txt, data/readme_088.txt).
  https://openarena.ws
  License: GNU General Public License, version 2 or (at your option) any
  later version (data/COPYING).
  The files are OpenArena 0.8.8's, from the release's openarena-0.8.8.zip
  (SHA-256 5a8faf7f5b51f351b0a1618c06b6b98a5f1a6758f1d39818de2c87df2a0bac4a),
  unchanged but repacked by tools/openarena/pack.mjs: data/oa-core.pk3
  holds the menus, weapons, items, effects, sounds, game code and six
  player models, and each data/oa-map-<map>.pk3 holds what one arena adds.
  The one file changed is scripts/bots.txt, which lists only the bots whose
  player models are included. Left out: the "mature" player models
  (pak2-players-mature.pk3 and the models in it), the mission pack, the
  demos, and the arenas and textures not played here. The level shots in
  data/levelshots/ are the arenas' own, converted from TGA to PNG where
  needed.
  The game code (the qvm files in data/oa-core.pk3) was compiled by the
  OpenArena team from the source in
  data/openarena-0.8.8-gamecode-src.tar.xz (OpenArena 0.8.8's game code
  release, as Debian distributes it: openarena_0.8.8+dfsg.orig.tar.xz,
  SHA-256 321c7811d78ffbec66dd7e2d61ce885d4199658c68a6b00c921d30a8cbef311e).
  The source of the art, maps and sounds, where the files in the pk3s
  aren't themselves the form for changing them, is in OpenArena's
  repository (https://openarena.ws/svn/source/assets/) and in Debian's
  OpenArena data source packages (the openarena-data, openarena-085-data,
  openarena-088-data, openarena-maps, openarena-misc, openarena-players and
  openarena-textures packages at https://deb.debian.org/debian/pool/main/o/).

